    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHi,\n\nin Neovim+Kitty, I would like to use the mouse for selecting text. With `set mouse=a`, Neovim also handles scrolling by itself. However, I do not like this Neovim-handled scrolling, and I much prefer the way Kitty handles scrolling (scrolling by pixels with the touchpad and also, scrolling without retaining cursor position, this is probably done by emulating the arrow keys). I also find it bothersome to enable the mouse and then disable it again everytime I want to select stuff with the mouse.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI would like to be able to use the mouse to select text in Neovim, without Neovim interfering with scrolling (with both the touchpad and the scroll wheel).",
