        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For reference, `:help 'mousescroll'` mentions \"You can disable mouse scrolling by using a count of 0\".\n\n```vim\nset mousescroll=ver:0,hor:0\n```\n\n> I get pixel-smooth scrolling with the touchpad, \n\nnvim has no knowledge of touchpad, so that must be a kitty feature\n\n> and scroll-by-3 when scrolling with the mouse wheel.\n\nyou could also try a `[count]` (e.g. `3` below). and you should be using `noremap`.\n\n```vim\nnoremap <ScrollWheelDown> 3<Down>\nnoremap <ScrollWheelUp> 3<Up>\n```",
            "created_at": "2026-07-21T13:45:28Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40889#issuecomment-5034814588",
