        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> you could also try a `[count]` (e.g. `3` below). and you should be using `noremap`.\n> ```vim\n> noremap <ScrollWheelDown> 3<Down>\n> noremap <ScrollWheelUp> 3<Up>\n> ```\n\n~~To be honest, I have no idea why this works but it does. It seems to me that this mapping should make it always scroll by 3 regardless of using the touchpad or the wheel, but instead, I get the smooth scrolling feature (that's present with `set mouse=`, implemented by Kitty), and the scroll-by-3 behavior when using the wheel. Anyway, I do get the desired behavior with this config. Thanks!~~\n\nNevermind - I forgot to do `set mouse=a` when testing the config.\n> It seems to me that this mapping should make it always scroll by 3 regardless of using the touchpad or the wheel\n\nThis part is correct, that's what the config does.",
